              <h1 style="margin:8px 0 16px 0;font-size:27px;line-height:34px;color:#071b31;">
                Join a Growing Connecticut Engineering Firm!
              </h1>
              <p style="margin:0 0 15px 0;font-size:16px;line-height:25px;color:#26384b;">Hello {{first_name}},</p>
              <p style="margin:0 0 15px 0;font-size:16px;line-height:25px;color:#26384b;">Our award-winning client is expanding its Transportation &amp; Traffic Engineering team and is seeking a Professional Engineer (PE) with strong transportation and traffic engineering expertise.<br>This is an outstanding opportunity for an experienced engineer who can work directly with CTDOT, municipalities, and public agencies while leading traffic engineering studies and transportation improvement projects throughout Connecticut.</p>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td style="padding:0 40px 23px 40px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;">
              <table role="presentation" width="100%" cellspacing="0" cellpadding="0" border="0"
                     style="width:100%;background:#f5f7f9;border:1px solid #d9e0e7;border-collapse:collapse;">
                <tr>
                  <td style="padding:18px 20px;font-size:15px;line-height:24px;color:#26384b;">
                    <strong style="color:#071b31;">Recruiting focus:</strong><br>
                    <span style="color:#b98500;">&#10003;</span> Responsibilities<br>
                    <span style="color:#b98500;">&#10003;</span> Perform traffic engineering analysis and intersection evaluations<br>
                    <span style="color:#b98500;">&#10003;</span> Prepare Traffic Impact Studies (TIS) and transportation planning reports<br>
                    <span style="color:#b98500;">&#10003;</span> Analyze traffic operations, capacity, safety, and signalization<br>
                    <span style="color:#b98500;">&#10003;</span> Support roadway and transportation improvement projects<br>
                    <span style="color:#b98500;">&#10003;</span> Coordinate with CTDOT, municipalities, and public stakeholders<br>
                    <span style="color:#b98500;">&#10003;</span> Attend public meetings and present technical findings<br>
                    <span style="color:#b98500;">&#10003;</span> Collaborate with multidisciplinary civil engineering teams<br>
                    <span style="color:#b98500;">&#10003;</span> Assist with project management and technical leadership<br>
                    <span style="color:#b98500;">&#10003;</span> BS in Civil Engineering or related discipline<br>
                    <span style="color:#b98500;">&#10003;</span> Professional Engineer (PE) license strongly preferred<br>
                    <span style="color:#b98500;">&#10003;</span> EIT candidates approaching PE eligibility may be considered
                  </td>
                </tr>
              </table>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td style="padding:0 40px 18px 40px;font-family:Arial,Helvetica,sans-serif;color:#26384b;">
              <p style="margin:0;font-size:16px;line-height:25px;">Send me the position title, location, compensation range and hiring timeline, and I will respond with the best search approach.</p>
            </td>
          </tr>
          <tr>
            <td align="left" style="padding:8px 40px 32px 40px;">
